ADDITIONAL PERMISSION (OpenSSL / AWS-LC LINKING EXCEPTION)

When Citadel is built with the `fips` feature it links the AWS-LC
cryptographic library, which carries code under the OpenSSL License and
the Original SSLeay License (GPL/AGPL-incompatible). An additional
permission granted under section 7 of the AGPL allows conveying that
combined build. The full exception text is in the LICENSE-EXCEPTION file
and applies to Citadel's first-party source files. The default
(pure-Rust) build links no OpenSSL-licensed code and does not rely on it.

